+++ b/rehearsal_toy/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Controlled multi-turn eviction test (synthetic, optional)
+
+A synthetic multi-turn visual QA task that isolates the problem RehearsalKV
+targets: later questions ask about image regions that Turn 1 never looked at.
+It is a mechanism test, not a substitute for ConvBench / MultiVerse on
+LLaVA-1.5-7B.
+
+**Status.** In the CPU sandbox where RehearsalKV was written, the small model
+learned the answer format but never reached visual retrieval (full-cache
+accuracy stayed at chance after 2,000-3,000 steps), so this test did not
+separate the methods there. On a GPU, train for much longer and only compare
+eviction methods once the full-cache model answers > 90% of questions.
+
+## Tasks
+
+* `make_needles.py` (recommended): six objects on a 12x12 grid (144 visual
+  tokens). Each object is ONE patch: a top-half key colour plus a left and a
+  right stripe, so every answer needs exactly one visual token.
+  "What color is the left stripe of the red block?"
+* `make_mtblocks.py`: four 3-patch objects (key patch, right neighbour, patch
+  below); harder, because answers need neighbouring tokens.
+
+Test conversations have 3 turns: T1 asks about object k1; T2 is a follow-up on
+k1 (50%) or a new object (50%); T3 is a new object (50%) or a revisit.
+Training conversations add a "Describe the image in detail." turn 15% of the
+time (the analogue of LLaVA's detail data); test conversations never do.
+
+## Model
+
+The repo's own `LlavaLlamaForCausalLM` (8 layers, d=128) in the evaluator's
+prompt format (`Q1\n<image>`, LLaVA v1 template, slow LLaMA tokenizer loaded
+exactly as the evaluator loads it). `VISION=analytic` (default for needles)
+uses a frozen vision tower whose patch features are the mean colours of the
+patch's regions, as LLaVA keeps CLIP frozen; `VISION=learned` trains it.
+
+## Run
+
+```bash
+# the repo's environment (transformers 4.31, torch 2.1)
+python rehearsal_toy/make_needles.py                       # -> rehearsal_toy/work/needles
+TOY_TASK=needles STEPS=20000 BATCH=32 python rehearsal_toy/train_toy.py
+#   resume: RESUME=<llm dir copy> RESUME_CLIP=<clip dir copy> SEED=8 CONST_LR=5e-4 ...
+bash rehearsal_toy/run_all.sh rehearsal_toy/work/runs 300 "0.0" "local_cache"   # full-cache ceiling
+bash rehearsal_toy/run_all.sh rehearsal_toy/work/runs 300 "0.9 0.8" \
+    "pyramidkv pyramidkv:--pyramid-exact-budget rehearsal_kv rehearsal_kv:--rehearsal-aggregation+max tgv_kv meda h2o local_cache"
+python rehearsal_toy/score_toy.py rehearsal_toy/work/needles/test.json rehearsal_toy/work/runs/*_predictions.json
+python rehearsal_toy/test_rehearsal.py                     # RehearsalKV correctness checks
+```
+
+`run_eval.py` runs the unchanged `eval_rouge_final2.py` with two test-only
+shims: fp32 on CPU, and the layer count read from the model config.
+`score_toy.py` reports exact answer accuracy by turn and by question type
+(t1, follow-up, new object, revisit).
